@startuml cbc-indexed-session-lifecycle
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam ArrowColor #455A64
skinparam ArrowThickness 2
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontColor #102027
  BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
}
left to right direction

title Indexed search session and its captured logical view

state "Search session" as Session #E3F2FD {
  [*] --> Ready
  Ready --> BorrowedSplit : borrow pending parent
  BorrowedSplit --> Ready : publish children and terminals
  Ready --> Scoring : take one original privately
  Scoring --> AwaitingPublication : exact verification
  AwaitingPublication --> Ready : publish rank / result
  Ready --> BuildingCacheEntry : begin scoped cache entry
  BuildingCacheEntry --> Ready : publish complete entry
}

note top of Session #E8F5E9
  Captured indexed view: contract + query + revision
  bind the root, original identities, buckets,
  summaries, payloads, and scoped cache observations.
  A newer published view does not retarget reads.
end note

state "Suspended" as Suspended #FFF9C4
state "Completed" as Completed #B2DFDB
state "Failed" as Failed #FFCDD2

Session --> Suspended : page or resource boundary
Suspended --> Session : resume same state and view
Session --> Completed : pending and private work empty
Session --> Failed : declared validation / failure result

note bottom of Suspended #FFFDE7
  Retain private phase, selected results,
  emission cursor, and cumulative ledger.
  Resumption does not reset or rescore them.
end note

note bottom of Session #E1F5FE
  This is a proof model for indexed operations.
  Standalone online automata have no indexed view.
  A disk snapshot is a separate persistence format.
end note
@enduml
